        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix: reconcile timed-out gateway message actions",
        "body": "Related: #80177\nRelated: #102179\n\n## What Problem This Solves\n\nFixes duplicate channel replies when a Gateway-backed `message(action=send)` exceeds the client deadline but succeeds later. The model can otherwise see a tool failure, compose a paraphrased retry, and make both deliveries visible. This was observed on Telegram after upgrading from an OpenClaw 2026.6.10 control window to the 2026.7.1 beta line.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nOn `GatewayTransportError(kind=\"timeout\")` only, callers with an abort signal repeatedly reattach to the unchanged `message.action` payload and idempotency key until the original action settles or the caller cancels. The Gateway already joins same-key in-flight work and caches its completed result, so every reconciliation observes the original action instead of dispatching another one.\n\nEach reconciliation wait is independently bounded to at least 60 seconds, while the caller-owned cancellation lifecycle bounds the complete operation. This covers multi-minute sends without returning an ambiguous model-visible failure after any individual wait expires. Call shapes without a cancellation lifecycle retain the previous single bounded reconciliation attempt so a permanent Gateway outage cannot hang a CLI action indefinitely. Definitive errors still return immediately.\n\n## User Impact\n\nAgents wait for the original delivery result instead of treating repeated client timeouts as send failures. This closes the timeout -> late success -> paraphrased duplicate path without lengthening normal sends or changing channel configuration.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- Sanitized production evidence in the related items shows a first `message(action=send)` timing out after 30 seconds, the Gateway later recording the Telegram send as successful, and a paraphrased second send following.\n- Focused regression coverage exercises two consecutive timeouts followed by the original result, verifies every reconciliation uses the same idempotency key, and verifies cancellation during a later reconciliation attempt.\n- `node scripts/run-vitest.mjs src/infra/outbound/message-action-runner.plugin-dispatch.test.ts` — 37/37 passed after the final rebase.\n- `node scripts/run-vitest.mjs src/gateway/server-methods/send.test.ts` — 138/138 passed, including the same-key in-flight join contract.\n- `.agents/skills/autoreview/scripts/autoreview --mode local --stream-engine-output` — clean; no accepted/actionable findings.\n- A redacted current-head Telegram live-proof request has been submitted to Mantis and remains pending.\n- AI-assisted. No private message content, chat identifiers, or credentials are included.\n",
